<title>FINLAND: MCDONALD'S SAYS TO MAKE 800 NEW FINNISH JOBS IN 97.</title>
<headline>MCDONALD'S SAYS TO MAKE 800 NEW FINNISH JOBS IN 97.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fast food chain McDonald's said on Friday it will open 20 new restaurants in Finland this year, creating 800 new jobs.</p>
<p>&quot;McDonald's will invest over 100 million markka this year in real estate, buildings and equipment,&quot; the chain's Finnish subsidiary McDonald's Oy said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;This year net sales are expected to be about 600 million markka,&quot; McDonald's Oy managing director Kim Hanslin said in the statement.</p>
<p>In 1996 McDonald's Oy created 850 new jobs at 23 new restaurants in Finland and had altogether about 3,400 employees at year-end, it said.</p>
<p>&quot;In the year 2000 there will be about 100 McDonald's family restaurants in Finland and the chain will have about 6,000 employees,&quot; Hanslin said.</p>
<p>--John Acher, Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 235</p>
</text>
